  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/0b5b5fdbd96d533abc66f5c2fbfbbe4a50d4ebe7</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/GioPalusa/itaLearn/commit/0b5b5fdbd96d533abc66f5c2fbfbbe4a50d4ebe7"/>
    <title>
        Remove legacy Italian writing-lesson stack
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-09T20:43:25Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16545448?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>GioPalusa</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/GioPalusa</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Remove legacy Italian writing-lesson stack

ContentView is the only entry point, and it routes to OnboardingView,
AdaptiveChatView and the MainTabs screens in LearningViews. HomeView was
reachable only from its own #Preview, which left the writing-lesson stack
hanging below it as dead code: LessonView, ConversationView (a wrapper
that just returned CurrentLessonView), LessonCatalogView, PaywallView,
the hardcoded WritingLesson catalog, and ItalianTutor with its
LessonFeedback and LearningMemory types.

LessonHistoryView stays. Despite sitting in the same stack it is live:
LearningProgressView links to it as &amp;quot;Tidigare skrivövningar&amp;quot;. It needs
only LessonRecord, CorrectionDiff and DesignSystem, all of which remain.

LessonRecord stays too, and the ModelContainer schema is unchanged.
LessonHistoryView still queries it, LearningStore.wipeAllStudies still
deletes it, and dropping the model would orphan the writing history of
existing installs. Removing it is a product decision, not a dead-code
cleanup.

The Xcode project needs no edit: it uses a file-system-synchronized
group. Package.swift drops the seven files from the target&amp;#39;s exclude
list; sources is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/72cc05ad44d5b48e3f459c2e393f2e5bbed7f6e9</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/GioPalusa/itaLearn/commit/72cc05ad44d5b48e3f459c2e393f2e5bbed7f6e9"/>
    <title>
        Rename ItaLearn to LangLearn and add multi-language support
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-09T20:42:52Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16545448?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>GioPalusa</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/GioPalusa</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Rename ItaLearn to LangLearn and add multi-language support

The app is no longer Italian-only, so the product name no longer fits.
Renames the app target, SPM target, test target, entitlements and asset
paths, and updates the docs and Milo build scripts to match.

Adds LearningLanguage: a curated list of teachable languages, each
carrying the speech voice, dictation locale and English name the model
instructions need, so the tutor is never inferring a language from a
bare code. The learner&amp;#39;s choice is stored in settings and LearnerProfile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
